  "summary_en": "Hong Kong ordinance amending the Road Traffic Ordinance to create a flexible pilot regime for autonomous vehicles. It prohibits AV use on roads outside licensed pilot schemes, empowers the Secretary to make a Pilot Regulation (licences, AV certificates, incident reporting), and allows disapplication notices and codes of practice. Autonomy is defined by SAE/GB Levels 3–5.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Section 136 bans use or permitting use of AVs on roads unless it is a pilot use or under a movement permit; penalty is a level 4 fine and 2 years' imprisonment.",
   "Secretary for Transport and Logistics may make a Pilot Regulation covering pilot licences, AV certificates, incident reporting and third-party protection.",
   "Backup operators (in-vehicle or remote) are treated as the driver by default; the Pilot Regulation may redefine who the driver is.",
   "Exemptions from traffic provisions require that safety is not undermined and an equally effective alternative measure exists.",
   "Autonomy is defined by SAE J3016 or GB/T 40429-2021 Levels 3–5, and the Commissioner may issue codes of practice."
  ],
